    "main_topic": [
      {
        "h_title": "Monthly Weather Summary",
        "main_title": "Monthly Weather Summary",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 3,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "In June 2026, Thailand\nexperienced rainfall throughout most of the month due to the influence of a\nmoderate to rather active southwest monsoon prevailing over the Andaman Sea,\nThailand, and the Gulf of Thailand throughout the month. This was accompanied\nby the monsoon trough periodically lying across Myanmar and upper Laos toward\nthe low-pressure cell covering Vietnam almost the entire month. However, the\namount and distribution of rain in Thailand were uneven, causing below-normal\nrainfall in most parts of the country. The average total rainfall in Thailand\nfor this month was approximately 8% below the norm, with most regions reporting\nbelow-normal monthly rainfall: the northern region received 19.0 mm (12% of the\nnorm), the northeastern region 61.9 mm (32%), the central region 16.8 mm (11%)\nand the eastern region 64.4 mm (25%) while rainfall was\nabove normal in southern region (east coast) 5.2 mm (4%) and the southern\nregion (west coast) 142.9 mm (43%). The monthly mean temperature in Thailand\nwas 0.4 °C above the norm. Further details are as follows:",
            "url": "https://www.tmd.go.th/media/climate/climate-monthly/june69.pdf",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.tmd.go.th/media/climate/climate-monthly/june69.pdf",
                "anchor_text": "Further details are as follows:"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
